237 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 49 0 R
/T (Record 1 \(no failed logins, daytime, known device, 35 MB\) is Normal for both models; the network probability of 0.193 is well below 0.50. Record 2 \(7 failed logins, 1 a.m., new device, 250 MB\) is Attack for both, but the network probability of 0.675 is only moderately above 0.50, so it is less confident, even though this record looks suspicious on three of four features. Record 3 \(2 failed logins, 11 p.m., new device, 850 MB\) is Attack for both, with a probability of 0.900; the large transfer drives this. The two models agree on all three records, which raises confidence in the labels. Had they disagreed, or had a probability been near 0.50, the record should be sent for analyst review.)
/E (Record 1 \(no failed logins, daytime, known device, 35 MB\) is Normal for both models; the network probability of 0.193 is well below 0.50. Record 2 \(7 failed logins, 1 a.m., new device, 250 MB\) is Attack for both, but the network probability of 0.675 is only moderately above 0.50, so it is less confident, even though this record looks suspicious on three of four features. Record 3 \(2 failed logins, 11 p.m., new device, 850 MB\) is Attack for both, with a probability of 0.900; the large transfer drives this. The two models agree on all three records, which raises confidence in the labels. Had they disagreed, or had a probability been near 0.50, the record should be sent for analyst review.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
238 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 49 0 R
/T (Why the simpler model may be selected)
/E (Why the simpler model may be selected)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
239 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 49 0 R
/T (On this split the Decision Tree reached 96% test accuracy against 80% for the neural network, with only one tree misclassification against five for the network. The tree is also explainable: its rules \(for instance, large data_transfer_mb, which has importance 0.546, followed by login_hour at 0.256\) can be read and justified to a security analyst, needs no scaling, and is cheaper to run. A neural network gives less insight into why a record was flagged. When a simple model performs at least as well and can be explained, it is the better choice here. A caveat: with only 25 test rows, a difference of a few records is not strong statistical evidence, so the comparison should be repeated with more data or cross-validation before a final decision.)
/E (On this split the Decision Tree reached 96% test accuracy against 80% for the neural network, with only one tree misclassification against five for the network. The tree is also explainable: its rules \(for instance, large data_transfer_mb, which has importance 0.546, followed by login_hour at 0.256\) can be read and justified to a security analyst, needs no scaling, and is cheaper to run. A neural network gives less insight into why a record was flagged. When a simple model performs at least as well and can be explained, it is the better choice here. A caveat: with only 25 test rows, a difference of a few records is not strong statistical evidence, so the comparison should be repeated with more data or cross-validation before a final decision.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
