/Title (This report answers all five questions of Lab 3 \(50 marks\). A 100-row cyber-activity dataset \(simple_cyber_activity.csv\) is split and standardised, a 4-8-4-1 dense neural network is trained for 20 epochs, its learning curves and test accuracy are interpreted, and it is compared with a Decision Tree. All numbers and graphs below come from an actual run of the code shown \(TensorFlow 2.21, scikit-learn 1.9, seed 42\).)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 254 0 R
/Next 313 0 R
>>
endobj
313 0 obj
<<
/Title (Note on the dataset: the lab manual refers to a prepared file that was not supplied, so I generated a balanced 100-row dataset with the same four features and label \(50 Normal, 50 Attack\) using a fixed random seed. Attack records are drawn with more failed logins, odd login hours, more new devices and larger transfers, with overlap between classes so the task is not trivial. Because of this, exact accuracies differ from the manual's sample figures \(about 76% / 88%\); the manual itself says results may vary.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 254 0 R
/Prev 312 0 R
>>
endobj
