417 0 obj
<<
/Title (Architecture. The input layer receives the four scaled features. The two hidden layers \(8 and 4 ReLU neurons\) learn combinations of the features, for example "many failed logins and a new device". The single sigmoid output gives a probability between 0 and 1 that the record is an Attack. Loss and optimizer. Binary cross-entropy is the standard loss for two-class problems because it heavily penalises confident wrong predictions; Adam adapts the learning rate for each weight.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 370 0 R
/Next 418 0 R
>>
endobj
418 0 obj
<<
/Title (Epoch = one complete pass of the whole training data through the network. Here 20 epochs means the network saw the training data 20 times. Batch size = number of records processed before the weights are updated. With validation_split=0.20, 60 of the 75 training rows are used for fitting and 15 are held out for validation, so each epoch has 60 / 8 = 8 weight updates \(7.5 rounded up\).)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 370 0 R
/Prev 417 0 R
>>
endobj
