425 0 obj
<<
/Title (On this split the Decision Tree reached 96% test accuracy against 80% for the neural network, with only one tree misclassification against five for the network. The tree is also explainable: its rules \(for instance, large data_transfer_mb, which has importance 0.546, followed by login_hour at 0.256\) can be read and justified to a security analyst, needs no scaling, and is cheaper to run. A neural network gives less insight into why a record was flagged. When a simple model performs at least as well and can be explained, it is the better choice here. A caveat: with only 25 test rows, a difference of a few records is not strong statistical evidence, so the comparison should be repeated with more data or cross-validation before a final decision.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 374 0 R
>>
endobj
